{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 MemoryAPI JSFX Repository\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A collection of custom audio DSP effects and JSFX plugins for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reaper.fm/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Cockos REAPER
}}}
, packaged for seamless installation and automatic updates via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55357 ?\u56550 ? How to Install via ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Ensure {\b ReaPack} is installed in REAPER (included by default in many setups, or downloadable from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
reapack.com
}}}
).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab In REAPER's top menu, go to: {\b Extensions} > {\b ReaPack} > {\b Import repositories...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Paste your repository URL:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/memoryapi/memoryapi-jsfx/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Click {\b OK}. ReaPack will fetch the repository index.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab In REAPER, go to: {\b Extensions} > {\b ReaPack} > {\b Browse packages...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab Search for {\f1 SpectralCarver} (or any plugin from this repo), right-click the package, select {\b Install}, and click {\b Apply}.\sa180\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55356 ?\u57243 ? Included Plugins\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 1. Dynamics / SpectralCarver\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Dynamics/SpectralCarver.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: 32-Band Dynamic Spectral Ducker with Cytomic State Variable Filters (SVF)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 32-Band SVF Dynamic Carving}: Frequency-dependent ducking that attenuates only the frequencies active in the sidechain, keeping the mix clean and preserving headroom without traditional broadband pumping.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Routing}: Route your kick, vocals, or sidechain trigger audio to {\b Channels 3/4} of the track.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Interactive Spectrum Display}: Visual real-time sidechain energy and gain reduction meters with draggable Low-Cut and High-Cut filter boundary curtains.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Redesigned Animated UI}: Modern design with hover halos, animated collapsible drawer, and selectable UI Text Zoom (100%/120%/140%) for HiDPI displays.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Stereo & Mid/Side Processing}: Switchable between L/R stereo ducking and M/S ducking (with dedicated M/S width balance).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Freeze & Audition}: Freeze the current sidechain profile into a static carving EQ curve, or audition the filtered sidechain signal.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Safe DSP Ceiling}: Hard NaN/Inf protection and anti-explosion audio ceilings.\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 2. Saturation / OInflator\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Saturation/OInflator.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Harmonic Waveshaper & Loudness Enhancer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Authentic Transfer Curve Waveshaping}: Specialized polynomial waveshaping algorithm that increases perceived loudness, warmth, and density without destroying transient punch.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Real-time Harmonic Transfer Viewport}: Live visual representation of the transfer curve and operating point with instantaneous boost dB readout.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Phase-Compensated Band Split}: Switchable 3-band split mode with 240 Hz and 2.4 kHz crossovers for independent multiband harmonic excitement.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Clip 0dB Protection}: Prevents signals from exceeding 0 dBFS ceiling when active.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Calibrated Studio Metering}: High-resolution input/output peak and RMS bar meters with hold decay and clip latches.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b HiDPI Text Scaling}: Quick toggle for 100%, 120%, and 140% UI text zoom.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Credits}: DSP algorithms by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/JClones/JSFXClones"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
JClones
}}}
, licensed under MIT.\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3. Saturation / Phoenix\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Saturation/Phoenix.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Analog Tape Saturator\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 5 Tape Topologies}: Selectable analog saturation types (Luminescent, Iridescent, Radiant, Luster, and Dark Essence).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 3 Brightness Curves}: Switchable high-frequency tape flux responses (Opal for neutral, Gold for warm, Sapphire for bright).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Input & Output Trims with Auto-Gain}: Input Trim (-10 to +10 dB), Process amount (0 to 100%), Output Trim (-6 to +6 dB), and optional automatic gain compensation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Studio Metering & HiDPI Zoom}: Dual input/output peak/RMS meters with OVER clip indicators and selectable UI text scaling.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Credits}: DSP algorithms by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/JClones/JSFXClones"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
JClones
}}}
, licensed under MIT.\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55357 ?\u56514 ? Repository Structure\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPack uses directory structure to organize categories in REAPER's package browser:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 .\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? .github/\line
\u9474 ?   \u9492 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? workflows/\line
\u9474 ?       \u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? deploy.yml          # Automatically regenerates index.xml on push\line
\u9474 ?       \u9492 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? check.yml           # Validates package headers on PRs/pushes\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? .reapack-index.conf         # reapack-index options\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? index.xml                   # ReaPack package index file\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? README.md                   # Repository documentation (shown in ReaPack)\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? Dynamics/                   # ReaPack Category: Dynamics\line
\u9474 ?   \u9492 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? SpectralCarver.jsfx     # JSFX plugin with ReaPack metadata header\line
\u9492 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? Saturation/                 # ReaPack Category: Saturation\line
    \u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? OInflator.jsfx          # JSFX plugin with ReaPack metadata header\line
    \u9492 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? Phoenix.jsfx            # JSFX plugin with ReaPack metadata header\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55357 ?\u57056 ? Adding New Plugins & Maintaining with {\f1 jj} (Jujutsu)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository uses {\b {\f1 jj}} (Jujutsu) for source control.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Adding a New Plugin\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Place your new {\f1 .jsfx} file inside the appropriate category folder (e.g. {\f1 Dynamics/}, {\f1 EQ/}, {\f1 Utility/}, {\f1 Synth/}, etc.).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Include the standard ReaPack metadata comment header at the top of the file:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 desc:MyPlugin (Effect Description)\line
// @description MyPlugin (Short description for ReaPack)\line
// @author YourName\line
// @version 1.0.0\line
// @changelog Initial release\line
// @about\line
//   # MyPlugin\line
//   Detailed description formatted in Markdown.\line
// @provides\line
//   [effect] MyPlugin.jsfx\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Commit your changes using {\f1 jj}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 jj describe -m "feat: add MyPlugin"\line
jj bookmark set master -r @\line
jj git push --bookmark master\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab The included GitHub Actions workflow will automatically run {\f1 reapack-index}, compile {\f1 index.xml}, and update the repository on GitHub.\sa180\par}
}
